  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="365d7ed2-3a76-509a-9e6e-5f1c2774178f" activityNameId="8c8d0150-b251-59e7-b91f-6ee92db1fc05" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, sludge from steel rolling, 20% water, to residual material landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, sludge from steel rolling, 20% water, to residual material landfill
Correction of Cr(VI) emissions according to "Chromium stability in Steel slag: Elizaveta Cheremisina and Johanna Schenk, www.steel-research.ch, steel research int. 88 (2017) No. 11. According to this literature the Cr(VI) composition of slag from BOF (basic oxigen furnace) and EAF (electric arc furnace) are 0.0001 wt %, 0.000001 kg / kg or 1 mg / kg.\nBecause of the fact that most of the Cr is in the Cr2O3 state. This values are based on model calculations.;
Synonyms: In UVEK2018 enthalten; 
UUID: d59e4bf5-0f9e-4654-871c-9e277330fcd1
&lt;null&gt;
Location: Switzerland
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data from literature
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_d59e4bf5-0f9e-4654-871c-9e277330fcd1.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
